>Everything you genocide reduces the possibilities on the
>Astral Plane.  Which is easier - an Astral Plane empty
>except for the Riders and those few ungenocidable species
>like titans, or an Astral Plane filled with wimpy monsters
>like vampire lords and balrogs that do little to a
>sufficiently mean character but block the riders?  On the
>Astral Plane, the more grid bugs and zrufties the better.

The only monsters I genocide are lich, demilich, master lich, and
arch-lich, which removes four frequency-1 monsters from the table. (And
to be honest, if I only had uncursed genocides available, I'd only
bother with arch-, master, and demi.) Nothing else is really worthy of
consideration except as a panic-button action.  I suppose genociding
';' might make sense if one wishes to insure against a certain subset
of water-related YASDs.

Genocidal mania (genociding as many enemies as you possibly can) makes
the game much harder because there will be vastly more titans, ki-rins
and Archons to deal with in the Planes.

Judicious use of genocide against a small number of particularly annoying
species makes the rest of the game easier without making the Astral
Plane *materially* harder.
